  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0189\" consists of 12 tables. The primary function of this schema is to store and manage various types of data related to music, including acoustic features of songs, information about albums, charts, popularity scores, artists, and their charts, and the releases of artists and their albums.\nThe \"acoustic_features\" table contains detailed information about each song, including its duration, key, mode, time signature, and various acoustic properties like acousticness, danceability, energy, instrumentalness, liveness, loudness, speechiness, valence, and tempo. The \"albums\" table stores information about each album, including its name, billboard rankings, artists, popularity, total tracks, album type, and image URL.\nThe \"album_chart\" table represents the chart data for albums, including the rank score, peak position, weeks on chart, and the week of the chart entry. The \"album_pop\" table provides popularity scores and information about whether an album is popular or not, along with the year.\nThe \"artists\" table contains information about each artist, including their name, followers, popularity, artist type, main genre, genres, and image URL. The \"artist_chart\" table represents the chart data for artists, including the rank score, peak position, weeks on chart, and the week of the chart entry. The \"artist_pop\" table provides popularity scores and information about whether an artist is popular or not, along with the year.\nThe \"releases\" table links the artists and their albums, providing the release date and precision. The \"songs\" table contains information about each song, including its name, billboard rankings, artists, popularity, explicit status, and song type. The \"song_chart\" table represents the chart data for songs, including the rank score, peak position, weeks on chart, and the week of the chart entry. The \"song_pop\" table provides popularity scores and information about whether a song is popular or not, along with the year.\nFinally, the \"tracks\" table links songs and their albums, providing the track number and release date, along with the primary key of the song and album. This schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary keys and referential integrity constraints, allowing for efficient data management and analysis.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves analyzing the evolution of popular music from 1964 to 2018 using data from both Billboard charts and Spotify. The goal is to understand trends in music popularity and identify influential artists, albums, and songs. This analysis includes examining musical attributes and their correlations with song popularity. An interactive Tableau Dashboard will be implemented for data exploration.\n\nObjectives\n\n1. Identify and analyze trends in music over time.\n2. Determine the most influential artists, albums, and songs.\n3. Examine correlations between musical attributes and song popularity.\n4. Provide interactive data visualizations through a Tableau Dashboard.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Music analysts and researchers.\n- Music industry professionals and historians.\n- General public interested in music trends and history.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Analysis: \n   - Analyze Billboard chart data and Spotify musical elements to identify trends.\n   - Compare and contrast attributes of top-charting songs and other hits.\n\n2. Data Visualization:\n   - Develop an interactive Tableau Dashboard to explore findings.\n\n3. Reporting:\n   - Generate reports identifying influential artists, albums, and trends.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance:\n   - The system should efficiently handle large datasets from 1964 to 2018.\n\n2. Usability:\n   - The Tableau Dashboard should be user-friendly and intuitive for all users.\n\n3. Scalability:\n   - Design should accommodate future data expansion beyond 2018.\n\n4. Security:\n   - Ensure the secure handling of any sensitive data or user information.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0189.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0189\nCREATE TABLE `acoustic_features` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `key` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mode` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time_signature` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `acousticness` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `danceability` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `energy` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `instrumentalness` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `liveness` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `loudness` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `speechiness` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `valence` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tempo` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `acoustic_features_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `albums` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billboard_rank` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_tracks` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `albums_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `album_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_of_entry` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `album_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `album_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity_score` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `album_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `artists` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `followers` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `popularity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `artist_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `main_genre` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `genres` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `artist_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_of_entry` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `artist_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `artist_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity_score` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `artist_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `releases` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `precision` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `releases_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `releases_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `songs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billboard_rank` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `explicit` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `song_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `songs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `song_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_of_entry` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `song_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `song_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity_score` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `song_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `tracks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `track_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tracks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tracks_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
